{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RED evidence and discriminating runtime proof.\n\nFull origin/main cProfile of the unchanged N=3000 real-git integration node: import_tickets 89.607s cumulative; 6,000 append_event calls; author -> _git_config 6,001 times / 47.790s; batch staging 3,000 CREATEs invoked sweep_stale_staging 3,000 times / 15.938s with 375,876 owner checks. Total pytest call time 90.033s (the profiler process later spent 52.6s deleting old pytest temp trees, excluded from importer attribution).\n\nIdentical-harness controlled A/B retained 3,000 creates, 3,000 comments and 29 total commits (5 init + locked 24 import delta): real counted collaborators 77.231s with 6,001 git-config wrapper calls / 3,000 sweeps; replacing only those collaborators with side-effect-free logical equivalents 16.404s, same state/commits. Delta: -60.827s (-78.8%), discriminating these two mechanisms from serialization/commit-count alternatives.\n\nFinal held-out RED oracle strengthens the existing N=3000 node without timing assertions. All original state/count/24-commit assertions passed, then the new collaborator tuple failed exactly as predicted: expected (author=1, sweeps=12), got (author=6000, sweeps=3000). The test was removed from the fixer-visible tree before implementation and is held by the orchestrator."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786640153575998001,"uuid":"c2577afe-8c58-4c12-9701-32d9940b27e5"}